    {
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Mara Voss:</b> Privilege is not the only road inward. Credential policy does the same work more quietly: it decides whether an ordinary staff account is a dead end or a stepping stone, and Northbridge has internal services that become reachable the moment somebody holds one.\n\nWe report the conditions that make guessing cheap. We do not demonstrate guessing, and I want that line visible in the write-up.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>languard policy passwords</b> in the terminal and read the policy review it prints.",
      "taskQuestion": "Which password policy weakness was found?",
      "taskCompleteText": "Correct. Weak length or no lockout increases cracking and guessing risk.",
