    {
      "persona": "Hacktivist",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Imani Vale:</b> This one is not abstract. Weak credential rules are the reason a clerk's account becomes the entry point in somebody's incident report, and the clerk gets named in it while the rule that failed her does not.\n\nNorthbridge either chose these settings or inherited them and never looked again. Either way it is an institutional decision rather than a personal failure, and the finding should say so.",
